Terminus is a city on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] and holds more people than all of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]: near sixteen billion by the last count [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] knew, though fewer souls than that number suggests. Its people wear machinery in the body, which they call chrome, and most are given it before they are grown. They keep no coin and no guard; credit is held and spent by some means a stranger cannot work, so a purse of gold buys nothing there.

The whole of Syrin is held in what its people call the Rhett, a dream that carries the planet's life in one weave. A visitor from another sphere is sick for hours when first set down on it.

Downtown Terminus holds the city's center, and there the corporation [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]] brings [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Media Con|Media Con]], its convention of the media made and aired across Syrin. [[Divinity/Immix|Immix]]'s talk show reaches the city, and [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] are known there as figures of it, with a small following.
